00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:20.135
[key chime: lookup cascade intercepts query] <v Narrator>First, advanced computing becomes affordable for everyone when expensive neural models act as a last resort behind fast local lookup tables, search indexes, and exact solvers. Second, compressing weights below one bit saves memory, yet unpacking them back to floating-point numbers at runtime wastes over eighty times more circuit-board energy than running packed integer logic directly.

2
00:00:20.295 --> 00:00:32.082
[low pulse: 5V board shunt baseline holds steady] <v Narrator>Third, one integer kernel checked by cryptographic hashes produces the exact same answer across processors, graphics cards, WebAssembly, hardware logic, and microcontrollers, halting immediately if a single weight changes.

3
00:00:32.242 --> 00:00:50.475
[lock tone: cryptographic kernel hash verified] <v Narrator>Across fifteen hundred deterministic control tasks, zero-model lookup beat neural baselines by 61.60 percentage points on structured tool schemas and 20.80 points on Boolean satisfiability at 1.41 to 2.09 microjoules net shunt energy, cleanly isolating the 12.80 point open coding triage gap.

4
00:00:50.635 --> 00:01:16.546
<v Narrator>On an AMD Kria five-volt board shunt with 0.09 to 0.11 percent idle drift, unpacking 0.1517 bits-per-weight matrices to 32-bit floats burned 63,335.56 microjoules gross—81.86 times worse than eight-bit integers—while packed integer Walsh-Hadamard, exclusive-NOR, bit-count, and nibble lookup dropped to 187.49 microjoules gross and 10.30 microjoules net.

5
00:01:16.706 --> 00:01:37.000
<v Narrator>One hash-verified integer kernel matched bit-for-bit across ten lanes and six fabrics—processor, Radeon 8060S Vulkan graphics, split processor-graphics, WebAssembly vectors, Verilog hardware logic, and a 1,444-byte bare-metal microcontroller—halting on single-weight tamper alongside 1,315 Planetary Digital Well lowering recipes.

6
00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:58.456
<v Narrator>End to end, the four-stage spellcheck cascade cut Kria shunt energy 26.58 times gross and 24.49 times net, cut Jetson Thor shunt energy 16.26 times, and avoided 38.46 times of stage-four calls. All receipts are Signed Provenance, Self-Checked—not externally peer-reviewed—with shunt, chip-counter, estimated, and unmetered joules kept strictly separate.
